TASK 2 - django_server
======================
Terminal output of the Django development server that powers the Cars Dealership
application, including the exact command line used to start it and the live request
log written while the local screenshots were captured.

Environment
-----------
  OS                : Windows 11 (win32)
  Python            : 3.10.8
  Django            : 5.2.6
  Django REST FW    : 3.16.1
  Flask (sentiment) : 3.1.2  (separate micro-service, port 5050)
  Node.js           : v22.19.0 (React source in server/frontend)
  Database          : SQLite (db.sqlite3, created by `python manage.py migrate`)
  Working directory : D:\Projects\CarDealership

Command used to start the server
--------------------------------
  python manage.py migrate            # create the schema
  python manage.py seed_db            # load 12 dealers, 12 makes, 50 models, 12 reviews
  python manage.py runserver 127.0.0.1:8000 --noreload

  (the sentiment micro-service runs next to it:
   python sentiment_analyzer/app.py  ->  http://localhost:5050/analyze)

